   1:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c **** /**
   2:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****   ******************************************************************************
   3:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****   * @file    py32e407_hal_gpio.c
   4:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****   * @author  MCU Application Team
   5:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****   * @brief   GPIO HAL module driver.
   6:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****   *          This file provides firmware functions to manage the following
   7:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****   *          functionalities of the General Purpose Input/Output (GPIO) peripheral:
   8:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****   *           + Initialization and de-initialization functions
   9:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****   *           + IO operation functions
  10:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****   *
  11:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****   @verbatim
  12:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****   ==============================================================================
  13:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****                     ##### GPIO Peripheral features #####
  14:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****   ==============================================================================
  15:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****   [..]
  16:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****     (+) Each port bit of the general-purpose I/O (GPIO) ports can be individually
  17:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****         configured by software in several modes:
  18:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) Input mode
  19:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) Analog mode
  20:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) Output mode
  21:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) Alternate function mode
  22:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) External interrupt/event lines
  23:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c **** 
  24:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****     (+) During and just after reset, the alternate functions and external interrupt
  25:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****         lines are not active and the I/O ports are configured in input floating mode.
  26:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c **** 
  27:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****     (+) All GPIO pins have weak internal pull-up and pull-down resistors, which can be
  28:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****         activated or not.
  29:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c **** 
ARM GAS  C:\Users\user\AppData\Local\Temp\ccDs4wtS.s 			page 2


  30:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****     (+) In Output or Alternate mode, each IO can be configured on open-drain or push-pull
  31:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****         type and the IO speed can be selected depending on the VDD value.
  32:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c **** 
  33:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****     (+) The microcontroller IO pins are connected to onboard peripherals/modules through a
  34:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****         multiplexer that allows only one peripheral alternate function (AF) connected
  35:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****        to an IO pin at a time. In this way, there can be no conflict between peripherals
  36:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****        sharing the same IO pin.
  37:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c **** 
  38:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****     (+) All ports have external interrupt/event capability. To use external interrupt
  39:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****         lines, the port must be configured in input mode. All available GPIO pins are
  40:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****         connected to the 16 external interrupt/event lines from EXTI0 to EXTI15.
  41:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c **** 
  42:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****     (+) The external interrupt/event controller consists of up to 28 edge detectors
  43:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****         (16 lines are connected to GPIO) for generating event/interrupt requests (each
  44:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****         input line can be independently configured to select the type (interrupt or event)
  45:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****         and the corresponding trigger event (rising or falling or both). Each line can
  46:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****         also be masked independently.
  47:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c **** 
  48:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****                      ##### How to use this driver #####
  49:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****   ==============================================================================
  50:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****   [..]
  51:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****     (#) Enable the GPIO AHB clock using the following function: __HAL_RCC_GPIOx_CLK_ENABLE().
  52:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c **** 
  53:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****     (#) Configure the GPIO pin(s) using HAL_GPIO_Init().
  54:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) Configure the IO mode using "Mode" member from GPIO_InitTypeDef structure
  55:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) Activate Pull-up, Pull-down resistor using "Pull" member from GPIO_InitTypeDef
  56:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****              structure.
  57:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) In case of Output or alternate function mode selection: the speed is
  58:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****              configured through "Speed" member from GPIO_InitTypeDef structure.
  59:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) In alternate mode is selection, the alternate function connected to the IO
  60:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****              is configured through "Alternate" member from GPIO_InitTypeDef structure.
  61:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) Analog mode is required when a pin is to be used as ADC channel
  62:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****              or DAC output.
  63:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) In case of external interrupt/event selection the "Mode" member from
  64:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****              GPIO_InitTypeDef structure select the type (interrupt or event) and
  65:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****              the corresponding trigger event (rising or falling or both).
  66:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c **** 
  67:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****     (#) In case of external interrupt/event mode selection, configure NVIC IRQ priority
  68:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****         mapped to the EXTI line using HAL_NVIC_SetPriority() and enable it using
  69:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****         HAL_NVIC_EnableIRQ().
  70:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c **** 
  71:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****     (#) To get the level of a pin configured in input mode use HAL_GPIO_ReadPin().
  72:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c **** 
  73:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****     (#) To set/reset the level of a pin configured in output mode use
  74:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****         HAL_GPIO_WritePin()/HAL_GPIO_TogglePin().
  75:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c **** 
  76:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****     (#) To lock pin configuration until next reset use HAL_GPIO_LockPin().
  77:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c **** 
  78:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****     (#) During and just after reset, the alternate functions are not
  79:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****         active and the GPIO pins are configured in input floating mode (except JTAG
  80:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****         pins).
  81:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c **** 
  82:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****     (#) The LSE oscillator pins OSC32_IN and OSC32_OUT can be used as general purpose
  83:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****         (PC14 and PC15, respectively) when the LSE oscillator is off. The LSE has
  84:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****         priority over the GPIO function.
  85:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c **** 
  86:../../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_gpio.c ****   @endverbatim
